    "updated_at": "2018-04-11T12:25:30Z",
    "body": "@jakearchibald it would only be a response. (If we go with rejection, we'd probably have to treat it as a network error. Only dropping the header seems too dangerous.)\r\n\r\n@bencebeky there's no way that I know of whereby you can set a request header value that contains a 0x00 from anywhere within the web platform. API-wise there's no way for response header values either, but I had forgotten to test this scenario (whereby the server sets it).",
